@startuml
' Rendered by scripts/build-diagrams.sh. Edit this file, never the SVG beside it.
'
' One neutral grey on a transparent background, so a single SVG stays legible on
' the light theme and the dark one. Nothing here picks a palette, which is what
' lets the site own its own colors.
<style>
document {
  BackgroundColor transparent
}
activityDiagram {
  BackgroundColor transparent
  LineColor #888888
  FontColor #888888
  FontName Helvetica
  FontSize 13

  activity {
    BackgroundColor transparent
    LineColor #888888
    FontColor #888888
  }
  circle {
    BackgroundColor #888888
    LineColor #888888
  }
  note {
    BackgroundColor transparent
    LineColor #888888
    FontColor #888888
  }
  arrow {
    LineColor #888888
    FontColor #888888
  }
}
</style>
skinparam shadowing false

start
:Decode\nYAML or JSON to an array;
:Detect\nread the OpenAPI version;
:Shape\ncheck the document's root shape;
:Cycles\nrefuse a reference that loops;
:Remote references\nrefuse a host the allowlist omits;
:Parse\nOperationExtractor resolves the refs;
stop

note right
  Every step collects faults
  instead of throwing. The
  caller decides what to do
  with them.
end note
@enduml